      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 458,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "These expressions all involve direction or suitability, but differ in usage. に向かって・に向けて describe motion or intent toward a goal or target, e.g. 'ゴールに向かって走る' ('run toward the goal'). 向き attaches directly to a noun and refers to the appropriateness or orientation of something for a group, without necessarily implying targeted action, e.g. '初心者向きのコース' ('a course suited for beginners').",
