      "attributes": {
        "id": 1219,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both relate to the idea of being suited to something else, but with different nuances. に合わせて・に合った implies active adjustment to suit a person or situation, e.g. 季節に合わせて洋服を選ぶ ('Choose clothes to match the season'), while 向き describes suitability or appropriateness by nature, e.g. 初心者向きの本 ('A book suitable for beginners').",
