      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1002,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both 向け and 向き describe suitability or orientation, but differ in nuance and intent. 向け refers to something explicitly designed or intended for a specific group or purpose, e.g. '子供向けの番組' ('a program for children'). 向き describes natural suitability without implying deliberate targeting, e.g. '初心者向きのコース' ('a course suited for beginners').",
